window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["01"]={"https://theconversation.com/australias-backpacker-visa-rules-are-changing-again-heres-how-the-new-system-will-work-296812":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"95db2f14b5e54fa74f18234c528c6bb8ff00f5be3dd6bced749bf69be9007237","read":"https://theconversation.com/australias-backpacker-visa-rules-are-changing-again-heres-how-the-new-system-will-work-296812","bytes":180044,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Australia’s backpacker visa rules are changing again. Here’s how the new system will work","by":[{"n":"Louisa Jones","r":"Lecturer and Discipline Lead (Migration), Thomas More Law School, Australian Catholic University"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T06:19:10Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["On Tuesday, Home Affairs Minister Tony Burke ",["announced","https://minister.homeaffairs.gov.au/TonyBurke/Pages/a-fairer-and-more-sustainable-working-holiday-maker-program.aspx"]," the government has backed away from plans to overhaul the working holiday visa framework. Burke says these new changes will make the program “fairer and more sustainable”."]},{"k":"p","s":["After announcing plans in September to significantly reduce the number of working holiday makers able to extend their stay, these new changes come after ",["criticism","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-01/business-and-backpackers-oppose-restrictions-on-visas/107323832"]," from regional businesses, employers and ",["workers themselves","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-24/backpacker-visa-changes-regional-work-less-attractive/107291720"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["So what’s changing? Let’s unpack the new rules and how they might work."]},{"k":"h","s":["What was happening before?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The government originally proposed introducing a ballot system to control access to second and third-year working holiday visas. With the exception of workers from the United Kingdom, people would only be able to stay in Australia if they completed their regional work and were randomly chosen from a lottery-style system."]},{"k":"p","s":["Burke ",["also announced plans","https://minister.homeaffairs.gov.au/TonyBurke/Pages/speech-national-press-club-17092026.aspx"]," to reduce the third-year visa allocation from approximately 31,000 to just 5,000 places."]},{"k":"p","s":["The changes were intended to manage migration numbers. The government has a net overseas migration target of ",["235,000","https://theconversation.com/australia-has-3-competing-migration-policies-the-problem-none-are-based-in-evidence-293945"]," by 2027–28. Currently, net overseas migration ",["is around","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/people/population/national-state-and-territory-population/latest-release"]," 292,000."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, regional employers ",["warned","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-09-18/working-holiday-visa-shake-up-alarms-qld-s-regional-businesses/107167986"]," that reducing the number of working holiday makers could leave businesses devastated and without workers, particularly in agriculture, tourism and hospitality."]},{"k":"h","s":["What’s changing now?"]},{"k":"p","s":["This revised plan is good news for working holiday visa makers. The proposed third-year allocation has increased from the proposed 5,000 to 25,000 places, while the second-year allocation remains at 45,000."]},{"k":"p","s":["Also, the proposed ballot has also been reshaped into a new process called the “Next Year Regional Work Guarantee”. Under this scheme, visa holders (except UK citizens) who want to extend their time in Australia will be required to register their interest and be invited to apply."]},{"k":"p","s":["Registrations are expected to open in December 2026, with monthly invitations beginning in January 2027. The government is yet to provide details about how the resulting process works."]},{"k":"p","s":["Notably, this may delay the processing of visas. If a visa holder wants to remain in Australia, they would ordinarily have to lodge a visa application before their current visa expires. This usually provides them with a bridging visa while the other application is processed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under the new proposed system, the working holder makers will not be eligible to apply for a visa until they have receive an invitation, delaying any necessary bridging visa applications as a result. This may cause significant practical implications for visa holders, including potential eligibility issues."]},{"k":"p","s":["Additionally, from March 1 2027, most working holiday makers seeking a second-year visa will need to complete four months of specified regional work, rather than the current three months. This will not affect visa holders currently completing their regional work."]},{"k":"p","s":["In short, the government has increased the number of opportunities to stay, but also increased the amount of regional work required."]},{"k":"h","s":["The skilled backpacker"]},{"k":"p","s":["The government’s response is understandable given the significant pressure to reduce overall migration numbers. Regional businesses rely heavily on working holiday makers, and these workers provide an important source of temporary labour in those areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the debate on this program overlooks something important: the people arriving in Australia on working holiday visas are not necessarily the backpackers we initially imagined."]},{"k":"p","s":["Working holiday makers to Australia can be 18–35 years old, depending on their country of citizenship. Many arrive with university degrees: ",["62.5% in 2021","https://www.flinders.edu.au/content/dam/documents/research/aiti/the-australia-experience-perceptions-of-australias-whm-program.pdf"]," had a tertiary qualification. Others have professional qualifications and years of employment experience."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, consider a qualified nurse, engineer or teacher who comes to Australia on a working holiday visa. To remain for another year, they may need to spend months picking fruit, working on farms or undertaking other specified regional work."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perhaps this is perfectly acceptable. This work is essential to many regional communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["But are we making the best use of the skills these people bring to Australia? The current system does little to recognise the new “skilled” backpacker."]},{"k":"h","s":["Better meeting everyone’s needs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Increasing the number of third-year visas is a welcome response to regional employers. However, simply increasing regional work requirements is largely a short-term solution to a much bigger workforce issue and a ballot system doesn’t seem to address this."]},{"k":"p","s":["In his National Press Club ",["address","https://minister.homeaffairs.gov.au/TonyBurke/Pages/speech-national-press-club-17092026.aspx"],", Burke said “we need immigration, we just need to make sure that it’s targeted to the needs of Australia in numbers and across the different categories that work for our economy”."]},{"k":"p","s":["With that goal in mind, the government should consider whether the working holiday program could do more to recognise the skills people already have."]},{"k":"p","s":["Could the new guarantee system take into account the occupations and qualifications Australia actually needs? Could working holiday makers with relevant professional experience such as healthcare or education workers be prioritised? And could there be a better transition from this visa to other employer-sponsored visas?"]},{"k":"p","s":["This need not mean abandoning regional work requirements or replacing existing skilled migration pathways. But it does mean thinking strategically about what to do with a stream of people who are often highly-skilled and want to stay in Australia for years at a time."]},{"k":"p","s":["A general ballot system may help control migration numbers, but it does not necessarily help Australia attract or retain the people with the skills it needs."]},{"k":"p","s":["We also need to remember Australia is competing for these workers across the globe. Working holiday makers have choices about where they travel and work (particularly if they’re highly skilled). If the process becomes increasingly complicated, requirements become longer and opportunities to stay become uncertain, they may simply choose another country."]},{"k":"p","s":["These workers ",["contribute","https://minister.homeaffairs.gov.au/TonyBurke/Pages/a-fairer-and-more-sustainable-working-holiday-maker-program.aspx"]," to local economies, support tourism and fill temporary vacancies across Australia. Perhaps it is time to stop thinking of the working holiday visa as simply a “backpacker” visa. Clearly, the people arriving in Australia bring more than a bag."]}],"chars":6244},"https://theconversation.com/an-inquiry-into-alleged-covid-19-vaccine-injuries-fails-to-weigh-the-ethics-and-risks-of-canadas-response-293333":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"f97d6ad968cc03f991d306ad8549c85ada5d30ef35c5f600276d0caae06c73c5","read":"https://theconversation.com/an-inquiry-into-alleged-covid-19-vaccine-injuries-fails-to-weigh-the-ethics-and-risks-of-canadas-response-293333","bytes":188513,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"An inquiry into alleged COVID-19 vaccine injuries fails to weigh the ethics and risks of Canada’s response","by":[{"n":"Kari Pahlman","r":"Research Fellow, Sydney Health Ethics, University of Sydney"},{"n":"Diego S. Silva","r":"Senior Lecturer, Sydney Health Ethics, Sydney School of Public Health, University of Sydney"},{"n":"Maxwell J. Smith","r":"Associate Professor, CIHR Applied Public Health Chair, and Director, Centre for Bioethics, Western University"}],"pub":"2026-10-21T12:18:21Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In early September, Conservative Party MP Dean Allison held a four-day independent, unsanctioned “inquiry” for “Canadians to ",["share their personal experiences","https://covidtestimony.com/terms-of-reference/"]," of injuries…from the COVID-19 vaccine(s).” The event ",["heard testimony","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ljt7046NEQ4"]," that alleged the response to COVID-19 was “a miserable failure,” not least due to the “assaults on freedom and other malign actions.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["An opinion piece in the ",["Toronto Sun subsequently","https://torontosun.com/opinion/columnists/allison-inquiry-resignations-public-inquiry"]," claimed that COVID-19 vaccine programs “killed thousands of Canadians,” repeating a call for an immediate stop of COVID-19 mRNA vaccinations, as well as “resignations, arrests and a full public inquiry…by the prime minister.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["It further claimed that Canada’s COVID-19 vaccination efforts represent, at best, the “biggest health policy mistake in Canadian history.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["But testimony heard at this inquiry — and responses to that testimony — conflate factual claims with ethical claims. As a consequence, it fails to recognize the ethical factors critical to understanding and justifying COVID-19 vaccination efforts."]},{"k":"p","s":["As public health ethicists, we’re interested in clarifying the factors necessary to substantiate claims about “policy mistakes” and informing expectations for future vaccination policy decisions."]},{"k":"h","s":["The conflation of facts and ethics"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some of the claims made in the Allison inquiry and related reporting pertained to facts, both stated and omitted. Other claims were ethical in nature. The difference is critical to understanding and justifying COVID-19 vaccination efforts."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, questions of facts are:"]},{"k":"li","s":["How many people were ",["injured or died","https://health-infobase.canada.ca/vaccination/adverse-events/archive/2024-01-19/"]," as a result of COVID-19 vaccination"]},{"k":"li","s":["How were vaccine candidates ",["tested and regulated","https://www.canada.ca/en/health-canada/services/drugs-health-products/covid19-industry/drugs-vaccines-treatments/about.html"]]},{"k":"li","s":["How many people were ",["saved by vaccines","https://theconversation.com/canadian-scientists-made-life-saving-contributions-during-the-covid-19-pandemic-190601"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Immunity and Society ",["is a new series","https://theconversation.com/topics/immunity-and-society-173768"]," from The Conversation Canada that presents new vaccine discoveries and immune-based innovations that are changing how we understand and protect human health. Through a partnership with the ",["Bridge Research Consortium","https://bridgerc.ca/activities-resources/the-conversation-canada-immunity-and-society/"],", these articles — written by experts in Canada at the forefront of immunology, biomanufacturing, social science and humanities — explore the latest developments and their impacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Getting on the same page about these facts and dispelling mis- and disinformation remains crucial."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, the ",["Public Health Agency of Canada (PHAC) records 455 reports","https://health-infobase.canada.ca/vaccination/adverse-events/archive/2024-01-19/#specialInterest"]," of deaths following COVID-19 vaccination, noting these deaths weren’t necessarily attributable to the vaccine. After assessing causality, PHAC reports a total of four deaths consistent with causal association to immunization. To put this in context, ",["more than 100 million","https://health-infobase.canada.ca/vaccination/adverse-events/archive/2024-01-19/#"]," COVID-19 vaccine doses have been administered in Canada."]},{"k":"p","s":["But getting on the same page about facts is not enough. That’s because claims about whether the government is justified in imposing certain obligations or burdens on the public — for example, requirements that citizens get vaccinated — are not answerable by facts alone. These are questions of ethics."]},{"k":"p","s":["These claims are about what one should do or what governments have legitimate authority to do, morally speaking: in other words, what is considered good or right or just."]},{"k":"h","s":["Values and policy decisions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Such ethical claims are a matter of values, which people or groups may prioritize differently. For example, in deciding on health policy options, some may prefer the option that preserves personal autonomy above all else. Others may prioritize fairness and the policy option that minimizes deaths or health disparities. And some may locate the preservation of autonomy in policy options that are fair for all and that saves lives."]},{"k":"p","s":["Critically, no policy decision is ever free of values and value judgments. All policy decisions, including those related to vaccination, involve trade-offs of competing values. That necessarily means there will be trade-offs in the distribution of benefits, risks and burdens experienced across individuals and groups in society."]},{"k":"p","s":["While evidence can tell us what those benefits, risks and burdens might be, it cannot by itself tell us what the right trade-off is. That is, whether it is ethically justifiable to limit autonomy in some ways in order to preserve autonomy in others or to protect certain segments of the population from severe illness or death."]},{"k":"p","s":["In other words, facts alone will not determine how those competing values should be balanced, what outcomes matter the most and whose interests should be prioritized, among other things."]},{"k":"p","s":["Discussions about the legitimacy of Canada’s COVID-19 vaccination efforts or determining whether it was the “biggest health policy mistake in Canadian history” requires not only solid scientific facts, but also explicit ethical reasoning. This entails careful analysis of the values at stake, how trade-offs may reasonably be made between those values and ultimately what governments are ethically justified in doing in the name of public health."]},{"k":"h","s":["The ethics of imposing risk"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fundamentally, the nature of the ethical claims made throughout the Allison inquiry and relevant reporting relate to one’s freedom to choose whether to be placed at risk by taking the COVID-19 vaccine. Yet, as our research argues, such claims about vaccine risks often fail to acknowledge or attend to the ",["reciprocal nature of those risks","https://doi.org/10.1007/s40592-026-00289-y"]," and the ",["reciprocal nature of freedom","https://healthydebate.ca/2022/11/topic/vaccine-risk-vs-vaccine-mandates/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the same time that we may be exposed to risk when getting vaccinated (since no medical intervention is entirely risk-free), we also impose risk on others by choosing to forgo vaccination or choosing policy options that fail to effectively address vaccine-preventable diseases."]},{"k":"p","s":["Just as having the freedom to engage in an activity necessarily entails accepting some of the risks that are created in doing that activity, imposing risks on others can correspondingly justify limits being placed on one’s freedoms."]},{"k":"p","s":["A useful example is driving a car: Choosing to drive means accepting risks to one’s own safety, and it also imposes risks on other road users. Those risks to others can justify restricting the freedom to drive at high speeds by imposing and enforcing speed limits."]},{"k":"p","s":["The existence of risk alone doesn’t preclude governments from implementing policy or health interventions. Every choice carries risk, including the choice not to act."]},{"k":"p","s":["While vaccines themselves do entail some small risks, they are used to reduce a much greater risk of disease that people may not be able to avoid or mitigate on their own. Vaccination policies are not implemented against a backdrop of zero risk, and so doing nothing — such as choosing not to introduce vaccination policies — also creates risk. In certain situations, such as pandemics, it can create more risk, and governments should be accountable for these risks as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some of the statements made at the Allison inquiry and in corresponding media coverage appear to hold that governments cannot impose risk on the public. From an ethical standpoint, this is not a given, especially when action and inaction both involve risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such claims need ",["further ethical analysis and reasoning","https://doi.org/10.1007/s41649-022-00218-1"]," that examines the nature of the risks and benefits, how they are distributed and the strength of the justifications used to defend policy action or inaction."]},{"k":"p","s":["Greater attention to ethics in policymaking and evaluation is critical to help identify the values at the heart of policy prescriptions, including related to freedom and risk, and to separate factual uncertainty from disagreement about those values. Only then will we be able to have constructive discussion about vaccination and vaccine policy in Canada."]}],"chars":7473},"https://theconversation.com/4-poin-revisi-uu-penyiaran-yang-mengancam-kebebasan-pers-dan-media-sosial-293853":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"e1c5efc6fc95b597d165953f206fb363fa60c91ab4888f284b5f30db15e94af9","read":"https://theconversation.com/4-poin-revisi-uu-penyiaran-yang-mengancam-kebebasan-pers-dan-media-sosial-293853","bytes":180079,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"4 poin revisi UU Penyiaran yang mengancam kebebasan pers dan media sosial","by":[{"n":"Senja Yustitia","r":"Dosen, Universitas Muhammadiyah Yogyakarta"}],"pub":"2026-10-15T09:14:39Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["● Revisi UU Penyiaran berpotensi memperluas pengawasan negara terhadap konten digital dan jurnalistik."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Ketidakjelasan standar, mekanisme sengketa, dan kewenangan mengancam perlindungan hukum bagi pers."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Pengawasan berlebihan berisiko membatasi pers dan hak publik dalam memperoleh informasi."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Revisi Undang-Undang Nomor 32 Tahun 2002 tentang Penyiaran","https://kpi.go.id/news/revisi-uu-penyiaran-didorong-lindungi-perempuan-dan-anak"]," kembali berjalan setelah pembahasannya ",["berhenti","https://www.kompas.id/artikel/tunda-pembahasan-ruu-penyiaran"]," pada 2024 akibat ",["penolakan","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4J2pmhcrKdA"]," masyarakat sipil, termasuk akademisi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meski sejumlah ",["pasal kontroversial dalam draf sebelumnya","https://www.kompas.id/artikel/daftar-pasal-kontroversial-dalam-draf-ruu-penyiaran"]," tidak lagi menjadi sorotan utama, revisi terbaru tetap menyisakan persoalan serius. Negara berpotensi memperluas pengawasan terhadap konten digital dan produk jurnalistik tanpa menjamin perlindungan tegas bagi pers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalannya bukan sekadar pembaruan aturan agar sesuai dengan perkembangan teknologi. Ketika batas kewenangan regulator tidak jelas, berita investigasi, kritik terhadap pemerintah, hingga konten media di media sosial berisiko menghadapi pengawasan dan sanksi melalui mekanisme yang tidak tepat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Revisi RUU Penyiaran: pengaturan dahulu, pembungkaman kemudian?","https://theconversation.com/revisi-ruu-penyiaran-pengaturan-dahulu-pembungkaman-kemudian-293209"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Revisi mengancam demokrasi"]},{"k":"p","s":["Saya mencatat empat aspek kontroversial dari revisi Undang-Undang Nomor 32 Tahun 2002 tentang Penyiaran ini."]},{"k":"p","s":["1. Perluasan pengawasan terhadap konten digital"]},{"k":"p","s":["Revisi ini menambahkan ",["definisi platform digital","https://www.remotivi.or.id/headline/meja-redaksi/871"],", penyelenggara platform digital, dan konten digital. Rumusan tersebut memperluas kewenangan Komisi Penyiaran Indonesia untuk mengawasi konten di luar TV dan radio, seperti konten buatan pengguna (user-generated content/UGC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dampaknya dapat menjangkau hampir semua media yang kini menggunakan platform Instagram, YouTube, atau TikTok untuk membagikan cuplikan dan rangkuman berita. Jika konten tersebut masuk ke dalam cakupan pengawasan KPI, media berpotensi mendapat pengawasan tambahan di luar mekanisme yang sudah berlaku."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kasus ",["pembatasan akses konten media Magdalene","https://www.kompas.id/artikel/tanggapi-pembatasan-akses-konten-magdalene-komdigi-sebut-siap-dialog-dengan-komunitas-pers"]," pada 2026 memperlihatkan risiko intervensi negara terhadap ruang digital. Saat itu, akun Instagram @magdaleneid memuat investigasi Tim Advokasi untuk Demokrasi (TAUD) mengenai penyiraman air keras terhadap aktivis HAM Andrie Yunus."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jika revisi ini memperluas kewenangan pengawasan tanpa batas yang tegas, intervensi terhadap konten jurnalistik berpotensi melibatkan lebih banyak lembaga."]},{"k":"p","s":["2. Risiko pengabaian standar jurnalistik"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Pasal 42 ayat (1) draf revisi","https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GZQdfsa69EDPPPGOeAEpMeQ2We6ZL6VV/view?usp=sharing"]," menyebutkan bahwa muatan jurnalistik dalam siaran dan/atau konten digital harus sesuai dengan Pedoman Perilaku Penyiaran (P3), Standar Isi Siaran (SIS), dan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Masalahnya, ketentuan tersebut tidak secara tegas menempatkan Undang-Undang Nomor 40 Tahun 1999 tentang Pers dan ",["Kode Etik Jurnalistik (KEJ)","https://storage.dewanpers.or.id/websiteprod/content/20250616033436-Buku%20Saku%20Cetakan%20ke%2022%20Agustus%202024.pdf"]," sebagai acuan utama. Padahal, produk jurnalistik memiliki fungsi berbeda dari konten hiburan atau konten digital biasa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan pasal ini, wartawan bisa menginvestigasi dugaan korupsi, mengkritik kebijakan, dan mengungkap penyalahgunaan kekuasaan tanpa takut dinilai berdasarkan standar yang tidak dirancang untuk kerja jurnalistik."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian tahun 2024","https://journal.unnes.ac.id/sju/imrev/article/view/78900"]," tentang kebebasan pers menunjukkan bahwa kebebasan pers di Indonesia menghadapi tantangan dari tumpang tindih kerangka hukum, termasuk UU Penyiaran, UU Pers, dan UU Informasi dan Transaksi Elektronik (ITE)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karena itu, ketidakjelasan standar dalam revisi justru berisiko memperbesar masalah yang sudah ada."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Apakah demokrasi takut pada ruang berekspresi?","https://theconversation.com/apakah-demokrasi-takut-pada-ruang-berekspresi-264829"]]},{"k":"p","s":["3. Risiko gugatan dan kriminalisasi semakin besar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pasal 42 ayat (2) ",["draf revisi","https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GZQdfsa69EDPPPGOeAEpMeQ2We6ZL6VV/view"]," menyebutkan bahwa penyelesaian sengketa terkait muatan jurnalistik dilaksanakan sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan. Rumusan ini terlalu luas apabila tidak disertai penegasan bahwa sengketa pemberitaan harus mengutamakan mekanisme dalam UU Pers."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Kasus gugatan Menteri Pertanian Amran Sulaiman","https://www.hukumonline.com/berita/a/tempo-digugat-rp200-miliar-oleh-mentan-amran-sulaiman--ini-duduk-perkaranya-lt68c912fae4bb2/?page=1"]," terhadap Tempo senilai Rp200 miliar terkait pemberitaan “Poles Beras Busuk”, misalnya, memperlihatkan bagaimana sengketa pemberitaan dapat masuk ke jalur gugatan perdata."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Kajian tahun 2023","https://repository.uinjkt.ac.id/dspace/handle/123456789/73856"]," juga menyoroti persoalan kepastian hukum dalam penyelesaian sengketa jurnalistik, termasuk risiko penggunaan UU ITE di luar mekanisme UU Pers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jika rumusan pasal tidak diperjelas, wartawan dan perusahaan media dapat menghadapi ketidakpastian hukum ketika menerbitkan berita yang menyangkut kepentingan publik. Ancaman gugatan atau sanksi juga dapat mendorong media menghindari isu sensitif, meskipun pemberitaannya penting bagi masyarakat."]},{"k":"p","s":["4. Posisi Dewan Pers menjadi tidak jelas"]},{"k":"p","s":["UU Pers menempatkan Dewan Pers sebagai lembaga yang berperan melindungi kemerdekaan pers dan menangani pengaduan terkait pemberitaan. Namun, revisi ini belum secara tegas menjamin batas kewenangan KPI dan Dewan Pers dalam menangani produk jurnalistik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kajian hukum mengenai disharmoni kewenangan KPI dan Dewan Pers dalam draf revisi juga menekankan pentingnya memperjelas pembagian kewenangan kedua lembaga tersebut. Tanpa penegasan, media berisiko menghadapi standar dan mekanisme pengawasan yang tumpang tindih."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemerintah dan DPR seharusnya menyelesaikan persoalan ini sebelum mengesahkan regulasi, bukan membiarkan media menanggung ketidakpastian setelah aturan berlaku."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ancaman bagi demokrasi"]},{"k":"p","s":["Polemik revisi UU Penyiaran tidak bisa dilepaskan dari kondisi kebebasan sipil Indonesia. Lembaga ",["Freedom House","https://freedomhouse.org/country/indonesia/freedom-world/2025"]," dalam masih mengategorikan Indonesia sebagai partly free. Sementara itu, Aliansi Jurnalis Independen (AJI) mencatat berbagai ",["bentuk kekerasan dan tekanan terhadap pers","https://aji.or.id/informasi/catatan-tahun-2025-pers-dalam-pusaran-otoritarian"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam situasi seperti ini, perluasan kewenangan pengawasan tanpa perlindungan kuat justru dapat mempersempit ruang kritik terhadap pemerintah."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian","https://drive.proton.me/urls/9DH1ZQNT20#CwaFhmXUU8bL"]," tentang pembatasan kebebasan berekspresi di Indonesia juga menunjukkan bahwa penggunaan instrumen hukum dapat menimbulkan chilling effect: orang atau lembaga memilih diam karena khawatir menghadapi konsekuensi hukum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dampaknya tidak berhenti pada wartawan. Masyarakat kehilangan akses terhadap informasi yang dibutuhkan untuk mengawasi kekuasaan dan mengambil keputusan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Polemik RUU Penyiaran: kebebasan pers indonesia terancam?","https://theconversation.com/polemik-ruu-penyiaran-kebebasan-pers-indonesia-terancam-230197"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Pengalaman Orde Baru menunjukkan bahwa kontrol negara terhadap pers dapat mengubah media menjadi alat propaganda, bukan pengawas kekuasaan. Di masa kini, pemerintah tidak perlu secara eksplisit melarang kritik untuk membatasi kebebasan pers. Ketidakjelasan aturan dan ancaman sanksi pun dapat membuat media membatasi dirinya sendiri."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karena itu, revisi UU Penyiaran harus menegaskan bahwa pengawasan KPI tidak mengambil alih kewenangan Dewan Pers atas produk jurnalistik. UU Pers dan kode etik harus menjadi rujukan dalam penanganan sengketa jurnalistik, sementara batas pengawasan terhadap konten digital perlu dirumuskan secara ketat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regulasi seharusnya melindungi masyarakat dari penyalahgunaan informasi, bukan memberi negara ruang lebih besar untuk mengendalikan informasi. Tanpa jaminan tersebut, revisi UU Penyiaran berisiko melemahkan kebebasan pers dan hak publik untuk mengetahui apa yang dilakukan oleh pemerintahnya."]}],"chars":6956},"https://theconversation.com/israel-has-voted-but-what-comes-next-dissecting-a-messy-ballot-and-coalition-building-process-295404":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"f2c05f969fa2c27728998f42ebb1db410e1b049c0343a5987222aa2cf85a7c65","read":"https://theconversation.com/israel-has-voted-but-what-comes-next-dissecting-a-messy-ballot-and-coalition-building-process-295404","bytes":193960,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Israel has voted, but what comes next? Dissecting a messy ballot and coalition-building process","by":[{"n":"Dov Waxman","r":"Presidential Chair in Modern Jewish Studies, University of California, Los Angeles"}],"pub":"2026-10-29T01:39:44Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Israeli election","https://apnews.com/article/israel-elections-netanyahu-eisenkot-arab-coalition-results-d4680e90210c9a8611853fda9d0deb61"]," of Oct. 27, 2026, was among the most highly anticipated votes in the country’s history. It was consequential, if not yet conclusive."]},{"k":"p","s":["With nearly all the votes counted, it is still unclear who will lead the country following the first national ballot since the ",["Oct. 7, 2023, Hamas-led attack","https://theconversation.com/topics/october-7-2023-146854"],", and the ",["devastating wars in Gaza","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/7/three-years-of-israels-genocide-in-gaza-in-numbers"],", ",["Lebanon","https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/political-instability-lebanon"]," ",["and Iran","https://theconversation.com/topics/us-iran-conflict-73960"]," that Israel has launched since."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Conversation turned to ",["Dov Waxman","https://www.international.ucla.edu/israel/person/2520"],", an expert on Israeli politics at the University of California, Los Angeles, to walk us through the main takeaways and the process and difficulties facing anyone trying to form a coalition government following a divided vote."]},{"k":"h","s":["What can we take away from the election results?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The first thing to note is simply the massive turnout – with ",["a 77.7% turnout","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/27/israel-election-turnout-highest-in-50-years-as-voting-continues"]," of those eligible voting, the highest turnout in more than two decades. That in itself is significant. It underscores how much importance Israelis attached to this vote."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before the election, many observers were saying that it was one of the most consequential – if not the most consequential – votes, and clearly many Israelis felt the same way."]},{"k":"p","s":["What drove this high turnout was different types of fears. Israelis of all persuasions were worried about how the outcome would affect what kind of country Israel becomes."]},{"k":"p","s":["The second big takeaway is that the ruling coalition, formed by Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu after the 2022 election, was resoundingly rejected by the majority of Israeli voters – well over 50% cast their vote for parties opposed to the current government."]},{"k":"p","s":["The five parties that make up Netanyahu’s right-wing and religious coalition went into the election with 68 seats in the 120-seat parliament. That same bloc ",["will now have 53","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cmdx3knq1xexo"]," – and that is a significant loss, no matter how Netanyahu tries to ",["spin this as a victory","https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/elections/2026-10-28/ty-article/.premium/netanyahu-claims-victory-without-majority-declines-to-call-for-unity-govt/000001a1-80ee-def6-abff-ccfe81460000"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It means that those five parties will not be able to form the next government, and as such, the vote stands as a repudiation of the Netanyahu government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Netanyahu’s Likud party will still be ",["the largest in parliament","https://nypost.com/2026/10/28/world-news/what-happens-next-as-israel-awaits-full-election-results/"],". But its share of the national vote declined, and it looks like it will have ",["six fewer seats","https://www.jpost.com/israel-election-2026/article-913164"]," in the next parliament, another blow to Netanyahu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Netanyahu’s far-right coalition partners fared worse than expected, too. In part, this was due to “wasted votes” going to a new far-right party that failed to make it ",["above the 3.25% of the national vote needed","https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israeli-elections-how-they-work-who-is-race-2026-07-29/"]," to be represented in parliament. Also, Likud drew some voters away from these far-right parties who had voted for them in the last election."]},{"k":"h","s":["What drove the Arab parties’ surprise showing?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The performance of the Arab majority parties – the more secular and left-wing Joint List and the more religious and conservative United Arab List – is very important."]},{"k":"p","s":["Combined, they currently look to have ",["increased their representation by nine seats","https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/10/28/record-arab-vote-brings-painful-dilemma-israels-opposition/"],", bringing their total to 19, a historic high for them."]},{"k":"p","s":["The reason for that is the massive turnout of Arab voters – much higher than the last election. But also, a less noticed trend is the increase in Jewish votes that those parties received. It is important to note that these are Arab-majority parties, not simply Arab parties."]},{"k":"p","s":["Aside from Netanyahu, it was also a disappointing result for the main opposition party, Yashar; its ",["leader, Gadi Eisenkot","https://theconversation.com/could-a-former-idf-chief-break-benjamin-netanyahus-grip-on-power-in-israel-293097"],"; and the anti-Netanyahu Change Bloc it was part of. The preelection polls suggested that the Zionist opposition bloc would do slightly better than the ruling coalition bloc."]},{"k":"p","s":["But Yashar ended up with over 200,000 fewer votes than Likud, winning a projected ",["21 seats compared to Likud’s 26","https://www.reuters.com/graphics/ISRAEL-ELECTION/RESULTS/akvelybkapr/"],", and the “Change Bloc” is heading to 48 seats, far short of a parliamentary majority."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ultimately, what is clear is that the Israeli public remains deeply divided. And the fact that there is still a good chance that Netanyahu will emerge as prime minister is remarkable given that many observers had already written his political obituary after the Oct. 7 attack."]},{"k":"h","s":["Was the vote a referendum on Netanyahu?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Certainly many saw this as a ",["referendum on Netanyahu","https://apnews.com/live/israel-election-netanyahu-gaza-mideast-news-updates-10-27-2026"],", Israel’s longest-serving prime minister."]},{"k":"p","s":["For his supporters, Netanyahu is the only person to be trusted with Israel’s security, especially given the threat from Iran. They ",["credit him for weakening","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/26/netanyahus-legacy-is-on-the-line-as-israelis-vote-in-the-first-elections-since-the-oct-7-attack-01136003"]," – albeit not defeating – the two non-state actors that most threaten Israeli security, Hezbollah and Hamas, and they praise him for ensuring President Donald Trump’s support for Israel."]},{"k":"p","s":["But for those who voted against Netanyahu, the fact that he has ",["refused to take any personal responsibility","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5zjx7xx3487o"]," for the Oct. 7 security failure – amid reports that he had ",["advance warning of a major planned Hamas attack","https://www.cnn.com/2026/09/08/middleeast/netanyahu-report-warning-uae-hamas-attack-intl"]," – factored into his poor election showing, as did his government’s refusal to ",["establish a state commission of inquiry to investigate","https://www.timesofisrael.com/court-doesnt-order-state-inquiry-into-oct-7-gives-government-2-months-to-decide-on-probe/"]," the Oct. 7 security failings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many also blame Netanyahu for not prioritizing the release of the Israeli hostages held in Gaza and prolonging the war there. He is also held responsible by many for the ",["precipitous decline in Israel’s international standing","https://www.timesofisrael.com/israels-global-image-is-in-free-fall-why-isnt-it-a-bigger-issue-in-the-election/"]," and for jeopardizing Israel’s crucial alliance with the United States."]},{"k":"p","s":["But it was domestic issues, rather than external ones, that motivated many of those who voted for anti-Netanyahu parties. Many fear that ",["democracy in Israel is under attack","https://democratic-erosion.org/2026/04/20/the-quiet-erosion-of-democracy-why-israels-political-crisis-should-worry-us-all/"],", and they particularly oppose the effort by Netanyahu’s government to ",["weaken the power and independence of the Israeli judiciary","https://www.npr.org/2023/03/27/1166200532/israel-civil-war-netanyahu-court-control"],", which sparked massive street protests in 2023. They also strongly resent that Netanyahu’s government has allowed ultra-Orthodox men to avoid military service, despite the Israeli military’s growing manpower shortage. And on a personal level, Netanyahu is ",["widely perceived as self-serving and dishonest","https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-18008697"]," – he is still on trial for corruption."]},{"k":"p","s":["Arab voters have other, more specific concerns that drove them to vote in record numbers, in addition to the Netanyahu government’s policies in Gaza and the West Bank, which they strongly oppose. Chief among them is the ",["soaring rates of violent crime","https://theconversation.com/palestinian-citizens-face-a-painful-choice-in-israels-election-to-vote-or-not-294000"]," in their communities, which the government – particularly the far-right Itamar Ben-Gvir, who oversees the police – has done nothing to address, say his critics. More broadly, many Palestinian-Arab citizens of Israel fear that if the far-right parties remained in power, their civil rights would be under threat."]},{"k":"h","s":["What should we expect next?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The key thing to underline is what happens on election day in Israel is just the first stage in the process of forming a new government. Since no party ever receives a majority of seats in the parliament, what really matters is what happens after the election when the coalition building begins. This can take weeks, if not longer."]},{"k":"p","s":["The party with the largest number of seats typically gets the first chance to assemble a governing coalition, but not always. Israel’s president, Isaac Herzog, will choose who gets the first chance to form a government based on who is most likely to succeed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Right now, it looks like Eisenkot will get the first opportunity, but his only real option is to form a minority government that would depend on the parliamentary support of the Arab-majority parties – which some members of his Change Bloc adamantly oppose."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite the success of the Arab-majority parties in the election, it is unlikely they will be invited to be formal members of any coalition – although that has happened once in the past, when the United Arab List ",["joined the short-lived government","https://time.com/6073019/mansour-abbas-arab-israel-coalition-government/"]," of 2021-22 led by Naftali Bennett and Yair Lapid."]},{"k":"p","s":["If Eisenkot is unable to form a government, then Netanyahu will get the chance. He could try to entice some leaders of the parties in the Change bloc to defect and join a right-wing government under his leadership, or a broader “national unity” government with a rotating leader. Netanyahu ",["did that in the past with Benny Gantz","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/in-israel-benny-gantz-decides-to-join-with-rival-netanyahu/"],", but then he later prevented Gantz from becoming prime minister – so I doubt Eisenkot would agree to do this with Netanyahu."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are reports in the media that the ",["Trump administration would like a national unity government","https://www.ynetnews.com/opinions-analysis/article/s1eio8k6mg"]," in Israel, so that might increase the pressure on Eisenkot to accept this outcome. And should war with Iran heat up again, that would increase the pressure."]},{"k":"p","s":["The most likely scenario, I believe, is that neither Netanyahu nor Eisenkot will be able to form a government, and a new election will be called, with Netanyahu as caretaker prime minister until that vote. Netanyahu has reason to hope that his bloc will do better in another election, so that may well be his game plan. In which case, it will be many months until Israel has a new government."]}],"chars":8546},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jordan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"469e7297df1cf5d6a6dd687aa3fdb0470b127f1dd7f466873d974e733d45b598","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/jordan","bytes":91590,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Jordan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-27T16:06:24+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Jordan-Syria border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 3km of the border with Syria."]},{"k":"h","s":["Shooting in Karak"]},{"k":"p","s":["A shooting took place at a Church in Karak Governorate causing several casualties on 23 October 2026. Follow the advice of the local authorities and monitor local media."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and US military infrastructure."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in, or planning to travel through, the Middle East should be prepared for possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to FCDO Travel Advice ",["email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jordan/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information, including updates relating to airports and airspace which could close at short notice"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around security or military facilities and strategic infrastructure. Recent attacks show that these areas may be targets or experience falling debris"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your departure plans under review, and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if advised to take shelter, stay indoors or find the nearest safe building or designated shelter. An interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection. The greatest risk is from falling debris caused by intercepts, and you are safest inside a secure structure. Do not approach or touch any drone or missile fragments or unusual objects"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jordan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Jordan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Jordan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Jordanian Embassy in the UK","https://www.mfa.gov.jo/en/embassy/London"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Jordan, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Jordanian dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British-Jordanian dual national, you can use your British passport to enter Jordan, but you must show your Jordanian passport when you leave."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Children with a Jordanian passport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children with a Jordanian passport, who are travelling without their father, cannot depart Jordan without a letter of permission signed by their father. They must have a letter even if they enter Jordan on a British passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Previous travel to Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If your passport has an Israeli stamp, you will not usually experience difficulties entering Jordan. If you have concerns, contact the ",["Jordanian Embassy in the UK","https://www.mfa.gov.jo/en/embassy/London"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Jordan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you wish to also visit Israel or Palestine and re-enter Jordan, you can get a multiple-entry visa from the ",["Jordanian Embassy in the UK","https://www.mfa.gov.jo/en/embassy/London"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visit visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can buy a single-entry visit visa when you arrive at a Jordanian airport or the Sheikh Hussein/North Border land crossing. It costs 40 Jordanian dinars (JOD) and is valid for 3 months. Some airlines may ask you to submit a health declaration at check-in. Check with your airline."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting for tourism, and you will stay at least 3 nights in Jordan, you can ",["apply for a Jordan Pass online","https://www.jordanpass.jo/"]," before you arrive. A Jordan Pass costs between 70 and 80 Jordanian dinars, which includes the visa fee and gives discounted entry to major tourist sites. You should only purchase a Jordan Pass from the official website. The Jordan Pass is valid for 3 months from date of entry."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["extend your Jordan visit visa online","https://eservices.moi.gov.jo/MOI_EVISA/faces/Pages/Runnables/login.jsf"]," for up to 6 months. You could get a fine if you overstay."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visiting Jordan for purposes other than tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Jordan for purposes other than tourism, you must apply for your visa in advance ",["online","https://moi.gov.jo/EN/Pages/Visa_E_Applications"],". This includes travel for the purposes of work or study."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Registering with the local authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to remain in Jordan for more than 14 days, you must report to the police station with a residency extension office that is nearest to your place of residence. You will be required to provide your biometrics (fingerprint and iris scan)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Failure to report within 14 days of arrival will result in a fine of JOD 200 to be paid upon leaving the country. This rule applies to anyone who entered Jordan after 1 October 2025, but not to holders of annual residency visas, tourists, pilgrims, or transit visa holders."]},{"k":"h","s":["Land border crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Jordan has land borders with Saudi Arabia, Israel, Palestine, Syria and Iraq."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Saudi Arabia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Those travelling to and from Saudi Arabia should refer to ",["Saudi Arabia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia"]," travel advice for the latest travel information including safety and security and entry requirements."]},{"k":"p","s":["The following three land border crossings between Jordan with Saudi Arabia are open 24 hours a day:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Umari (AlOmari) Border Crossing: Primary crossing, approximately 155 km from Amman"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mudawara (AlMudawwara) Border Crossing: Located farther east, approximately 322 km from Amman"]},{"k":"li","s":["AlDurra Crossing (opposite Haql): Connecting Aqaba with the Saudi city of Haql"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entry to Saudi Arabia"]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals who are trying to leave Jordan via Saudi Arabia and who are travelling on British Emergency Travel Documents, Emergency Passports, or passports with less than 6 months remaining validity, should call the helplines for British Embassy Riyadh +966 (0) 11481 9100 or British Consulate Jeddah +966 (0)126225550 for advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Those traveling from Israel or Palestine should refer to ",["Israel’s travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel"]," and ",["Palestine’s travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/palestine"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The three land border crossings from Israel and Palestine are open most days from 8 or 8.30am. Closures may happen at no notice, including over the weekend."]},{"k":"li","s":["King Hussein/Allenby Bridge"]},{"k":"li","s":["The Northern (Sheikh Hussein/Jordan River Crossing) crossing"]},{"k":"li","s":["The Southern (Wadi Araba/Yitzhak Rabin) crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["The King Hussein Bridge/Allenby crossing is not an international crossing between Jordan and Palestine or Israel. You cannot enter Jordan using the King Hussein Bridge/Allenby crossing without getting a visa beforehand. You can get a visa from the ",["Jordanian Ministry of Interior","https://eservices.moi.gov.jo/MOI_EVISA/faces/Pages/Runnables/login.jsf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling on a British passport, you do not need to prebook to leave Jordan via the King Hussein/Allenby Bridge."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have entered Jordan using a non-British passport you may need to prebook to enter Israel or Palestine via the King Hussein/Allenby Bridge. Bookings are made via ",["Jordan Express Tourist Transport Company","https://jett-khb.com.jo/about"],", at busy times they can be booked up several days in advance."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you wish to combine travel to Jordan with a visit to Israel or Palestine, you can get a multiple-entry visa before you travel from the ",["Jordanian Ministry of Interior","https://eservices.moi.gov.jo/MOI_EVISA/faces/Pages/Runnables/login.jsf"],". You should also check the ",["Israel travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel"]," before using the land borders to enter Israel."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the Jordanian side, border guards will stamp passports unless the traveller requests otherwise and tells them before they hand over their passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Photography and videography are not permitted on the border crossings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Syria"]},{"k":"p","s":["The FCDO advises against all travel to Syria."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Iraq"]},{"k":"p","s":["The FCDO advises against all travel to Iraq ."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea Crossing to Egypt"]},{"k":"p","s":["Those traveling to and from Egypt should refer to ",["Egypt travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt"]," for the latest travel information including safety and security and entry requirements."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ferry services operate between Aqaba and Egypt (Taba Heights and Nuweiba). Contact ferry operators directly for schedules and availability."]},{"k":"h","s":["Departure tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must pay a departure tax of 10 Jordanian dinars in cash at all land border crossings. There are usually ATMs at the border."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Jordan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/115/jordan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health screening"]},{"k":"hs","s":["HIV test"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a HIV test if you are staying in Jordan for more than 30 days. It costs 20 Jordanian dinars to get the health certificate."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Jordan. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must ",["apply for approval to take a drone","https://carc.gov.jo/en/drones"]," into Jordan at least 10 working days before you travel. If you have not received a permit before you arrive, the authorities will hold your drone at the airport. You can collect it when you leave Jordan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Jordan","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jordan/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Jordan"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the context of regional escalation, Iran-aligned militia groups have threatened to target US interests across the region, have claimed attacks in Jordan and are likely to continue to carry out these attacks in Jordan."]},{"k":"p","s":["As was the case before the recent regional escalation, terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Jordan, including in places visited by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping malls"]},{"k":"li","s":["restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourist sites"]},{"k":"li","s":["border crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of significant attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2025, 2 people and the assailant were killed in a knife attack at the King Hussein/Allenby bridge"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2024, there were 3 separate attacks on the border crossings, where 3 Israeli border personnel were killed"]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political situation in Jordan is stable but sometimes there are protests in Amman and other cities. You should stay away from demonstrations and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Demonstrations and mass gatherings"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 23 June 2026, large crowds gathered to watch Jordan’s national team play in the 2026 World Cup. One person died and eight were injured in downtown Amman at a public screening of the match."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay aware of your surroundings and consider avoiding crowds, crowd control measures may be limited"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media"]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are generally low, but there is a risk of pickpocketing, bag-snatching and theft from cars. Stay alert and keep your money, passport and valuables secure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Street begging can be aggressive, particularly in areas frequented by foreigners. Do not engage with beggars."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in popular travel destinations around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Drink Spiking and Methanol Poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when walking or travelling alone. Maintain at least the same level of personal security awareness as you would in the UK. See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should not accept lifts from strangers. If you must use a taxi , you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask your hotel to recommend a reliable driver"]},{"k":"li","s":["not ride in the front seat, particularly when travelling alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["use Uber or Careem which are safer than yellow taxis"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Jordan is a predominantly Islamic country. Always respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions so you do not cause offence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["The police carry out random security checks. Keep ID (passport or driving licence) with you to show at checkpoints."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to drink alcohol on the street, but you can drink in bars, clubs, hotels and private homes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to possess, use or traffic drugs. If convicted, you can get a lengthy prison sentence and heavy fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual relations are not illegal, but same-sex couples showing affection in public may cause offence. You could be arrested under other Jordanian laws. Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Unmarried couples living together"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is socially unacceptable for unmarried foreign couples to live together. Some landlords may ask if you are married or request a marriage certificate."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Converting people to Christianity"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to encourage someone to convert to Christianity. You could face a prison sentence or a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visiting Petra"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Petra Archaeological Park has strict visitor opening and closing hours. You risk arrest and prosecution if you are in the park outside of these hours. Tourists have been locked in Petra overnight."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ask the tourist office staff if you’re unclear about ticket prices and before agreeing to additional charges."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cash machines are only widely available in Amman and other major towns and cities. Most places accept card payments."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["For all activities, bring appropriate clothing and enough food and water for extreme temperatures."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tour operators"]},{"k":"p","s":["The quality of tour operators providing outdoor activities varies. A list of all tour operators is available on the ",["Visit Jordan","https://international.visitjordan.com/page/26/Tour-Operators"]," website. Research tour operators and choose one with suitable safety mitigations and insurance in place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visiting wadis"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are around 80 wadis (valleys) in Jordan. During the rainy season from November to March there’s a risk of flash floods. Before travelling to a wadi, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the weather forecast"]},{"k":"li","s":["not travel to places after heavy rain for at least one day"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re caught in a flash flood, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["go to a high point"]},{"k":"li","s":["not attempt to cross the water"]},{"k":"li","s":["try to drive to a dry spot"]},{"k":"li","s":["contact Civil Defence on 911 if you need help"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving and snorkelling"]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety standards of diving operators in Aqaba can vary. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not dive or snorkel alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["make bookings through your tour representative"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure the operator has a recognised accreditation, like PADI"]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Jordan, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards differ from those in the UK. Stray animals, broken-down vehicles and unmarked roadworks are common. There have been fatal accidents on the Desert Highway. Drive with care at night and avoid unlit roads."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rules of the road"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have an accident, do not leave the scene before the police arrive and take a statement. Call 911 to contact police."]},{"k":"p","s":["The speed limit varies from 40kph in some urban areas to 120kph on some highways. You should follow speed restrictions carefully. The police issue 15 to 150 Jordanian dinar on-the-spot fines."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drive or ride in a front seat without a seatbelt or use a mobile phone while driving. You could get a fine. All cars must carry a fire extinguisher and warning triangle."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving in winter"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy snow can trap vehicles and block mountain roads, including around Petra. Take care and follow local restrictions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the rainy season from November to March, the Jordanian government sometimes issues flood alerts, particularly along the Jordan Valley. Flood alerts can cause diversions and road closures, affecting drivers and hikers. There is a risk of flash flooding. Be alert to advisories and co-operate with the authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Jordan. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jordan"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jordan/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional hostilities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following regional hostilities with Iran and in Israel, Lebanon, the West Bank and Gaza, the security situation could change suddenly."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you hear sirens, remain indoors and stay away from windows to ensure protection from any possible missile/drone fragments. If there are any injuries or damages, call 911 immediately."]},{"k":"h","s":["Land border crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["The roads within Jordan and land border crossings between Jordan and Israel and the West Bank can close at no notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["Israel travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel"]," and ",["Palestine travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/palestine"]," and check with the Jordanian authorities before crossing."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care near borders and if you’re crossing into a neighbouring country. Jordanian army and police units patrol the borders with Syria and Iraq and check traffic."]},{"k":"p","s":["There may be landmines near borders and military installations. Minefields are usually fenced off and marked, but fences and signs may be in a poor state of repair."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Jordan-Syria border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 3km of the border with Syria. The situation in southern Syria is fragile and instability or terrorist activity could start with little or no notice. There are also reports of violent confrontations between smugglers and the Jordan Armed Forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Jaber land border crossing from Jordan into Syria has reopened. Jordanian nationals may use the crossing to return to Jordan from Syria, and Syrian citizens holding a valid Syrian passport or travel document from the Syrian Embassy in Amman may use the crossing to return to Syria. There may be a heavier than usual military presence along the border."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Jordan-Iraq border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the provinces in Iraq bordering Jordan. See ",["Iraq travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iraq"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Jordan-Israel border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the conflict in Israel and Palestine, there have been instances of protests near the border on Fridays. Be particularly cautious in areas close to the border."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Jordan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/115/jordan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Jordan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/115/jordan"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["biting insects and ticks"]},{"k":"li","s":["Middle East respiratory syndrome coronavirus"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Jordan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities outside Amman and Aqaba are basic. In an emergency you should seek treatment in Amman or Aqaba."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Jordan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-practitioners-in-amman"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Jordan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Thefts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your insurer may require a police report or crime reference number if you want to make a claim. This usually means you need to report the theft while you are still in the country. If your passport is stolen you must ",["cancel it as soon as possible","https://www.gov.uk/report-a-lost-or-stolen-passport"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Jordan"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=jordan"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=jordan"]," in Jordan"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Jordan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/jordan-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Jordan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/jordan-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/jordan/british-embassy-amman"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jordan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Jordan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-jordan"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":23283,"change":"Updated information about regional tensions (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/north-korea":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"e10af9a9798375a3d21129b443edf2d73eb5009b38620907a5fb46463c7a3bb4","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/north-korea","bytes":40434,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Korea, DPR (North Korea) travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-08T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-10T13:22:30+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to North Korea"]},{"k":"p","s":["The level of tension on the Korean Peninsula remains high. While daily life in the capital city, Pyongyang, may appear calm, the security situation in North Korea can change quickly with no advance warning about possible actions by the authorities. This poses significant risks to British visitors and residents. See ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/north-korea/safety-and-security#political-situation"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Border restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["North Korea’s borders have been closed to general entry since the government imposed COVID-19 border restrictions in 2020."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government has recently started to relax the COVID restrictions. As a result, some embassies have resumed normal operations and some limited tourism has restarted."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the North Korean government has not resumed all passenger routes into and out of North Korea. Many embassies – including the British Embassy in Pyongyang – remain closed."]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from the UK government"]},{"k":"p","s":["The North Korean authorities have previously detained foreign nationals for allegedly violating local laws and have denied them access to support from their governments."]},{"k":"p","s":["The few British people who visit North Korea are usually part of an organised tour. If you decide to visit North Korea against FCDO advice, follow the guidance of your tour operator and the local authorities. Failure to do so could put your personal safety at risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Support from FCDO is severely limited, especially while there is no British Embassy presence. Remote support is available if you’re able to ",["contact us online","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/home"]," or by phone. However, the routine lack of access to internet and mobile networks makes it almost impossible to communicate outside of North Korea. See ",["Getting help","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/north-korea/getting-help"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel against FCDO advice, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/north-korea/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of North Korea’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in North Korea set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the North Korean Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Email: prkinfo@yahoo.com"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 8992 4965"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists can normally only travel to North Korea as part of an organised tour. Independent travellers will need a sponsor and permission from the Ministry for Foreign Affairs."]},{"k":"h","s":["COVID-19 rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["North Korea’s borders have been closed to general entry since the government imposed COVID-19 border restrictions in 2020. To check the latest restrictions and testing requirements, contact the North Korean Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport should be valid for the proposed duration of your stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements, including for China if you are travelling through China. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter North Korea."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Send visa applications and enquires directly to the North Korean Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Email: prkinfo@yahoo.com"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 8992 4965"]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter North Korea, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s North Korea guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/119/north-korea#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must be registered with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs if your visit is for more than 24 hours. Most hotels will complete this process on your behalf."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some hotels may insist on full cash payment in advance when you check in."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can bring a foreign mobile phone into the country, but you must register it at the border. There is no connectivity to international or domestic mobile networks from within North Korea using an international SIM card."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must leave any Global Positioning System technology with North Korean customs. You can collect your devices when you leave North Korea."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid bringing books or other written material in the Korean language, including anything with religious content. Consider carefully any films or television programmes that you bring into the country, either on DVD or on data storage devices. Customs officers will confiscate any literature or media deemed to have an anti-government message or deemed subversive or pornographic. There could be further severe penalties including imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["The North Korean authorities also impose restrictions and harsh penalties on their own citizens if they are found in possession of foreign media."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been cases of travel guides being confiscated at the airport on arrival and given back on departure."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into and out of North Korea"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import or export the North Korean currency – won. There are no restrictions on importing and exporting foreign currency, but you must declare it at customs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shops and restaurants list their prices in won, but usually charge foreign nationals in foreign currency. They convert the won price using official exchange rates."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US dollar and the euro are the most widely accepted currencies, although some places accept Chinese yuan (‘Renminbi’)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit cards and international mobile payments are not accepted."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in North Korea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in North Korea, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The level of tension on the Korean peninsula remains high. Political negotiations between North Korea and the United States in 2018 to 2019 broke down and have not resumed. North and South Korea agreed a set of security guidelines in 2019 to reduce the risk of accidental cross-border conflict, but both sides have now withdrawn from this agreement."]},{"k":"p","s":["In late 2023, the North Korean government changed its reunification policy, leading to increased tensions with South Korea. North Korea continues to develop nuclear weapons and ballistic missiles, although these are banned by UN Security Council resolutions. North Korea’s material and political support for Russia’s illegal invasion of Ukraine has further strained relations with much of the international community."]},{"k":"p","s":["Inter-Korean tensions usually rise around the time of South Korean-US military exercises, often held in the spring and autumn."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Nuclear and missile tests"]},{"k":"p","s":["North Korea carried out 6 underground nuclear tests between 2006 and 2017 and has stated that it reserves the right to carry out further tests."]},{"k":"p","s":["North Korea also regularly conducts ballistic missile test launches, sometimes without giving the required notice to international aviation authorities, and against UN Security Council resolutions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime against foreign nationals in North Korea is rare. Take sensible precautions to protect your belongings."]},{"k":"h","s":["Fire safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Levels of fire safety awareness may be low. Check hotel fire procedures with the hotel reception or consult your tour operator."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care with your words and actions during your stay. Insults or jokes about the North Korean political system and its leadership are taken very seriously. Offences that would be considered trivial in other countries can incur very severe penalties in North Korea. This includes the promotion of other religions or beliefs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Arrests and trials"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals may face arrest for not paying sufficient respect, including not treating images of the current and former North Korean leaders with care."]},{"k":"p","s":["The North Korean authorities have previously arrested visitors with or without specified charges, including 4 US citizens and one Canadian citizen. Some have faced public trials and imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2016 a US national was convicted of ‘crimes against the state’ and sentenced to 15 years of hard labour. The court had found him guilty of attempting to steal a political banner from the staff quarters of a tourist hotel. He fell into a coma while in detention and was released in 2017, but died soon after his return to the US."]},{"k":"p","s":["If arrested, you are not guaranteed access to phone calls with family and friends or the British Embassy, or to independent legal advice or interpretation services."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking photos or videos"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ask permission from your tour guide before taking any photographs. Avoid pointing cameras at North Korean officials or guarded buildings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no specific legislation outlawing same-sex relationships in North Korea, the authorities do not recognise same-sex rights and consider same-sex relationships and behaviours unacceptable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel outside Pyongyang"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals living in Pyongyang are normally allowed to travel within the city, but usually require permission to travel outside Pyongyang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel for visitors within North Korea is severely restricted. Whether you are visiting on business or as a tourist, a guide will almost always accompany you. The guide will decide where you can go. It is your guide’s responsibility to get permission to travel outside Pyongyang. Military checkpoints on entry and exit to all towns usually include ID checks."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2008 guards shot and killed a South Korean tourist who strayed into a restricted military area. Remain in permitted areas and move away immediately if asked to do so by North Korean officials."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get taxis from hotels or outside some department stores, but they will be reluctant to take you without a local guide or interpreter. Foreign nationals are not usually allowed to use public transport unless they are accompanied by a local guide."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to drive in North Korea, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". International driving permits are not valid in North Korea. Foreign nationals living in North Korea must get a local driving licence by passing a local driving test."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should take extra care when driving, as roads are often of poor quality with frequent hazards, and pedestrian road safety awareness is low. In 2018 a tour bus carrying Chinese tourists crashed on the road between Pyongyang and the Demilitarized Zone, killing a number of passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most travellers entering North Korea by air take direct flights from Beijing to Pyongyang operated by the North Korean national airline, Air Koryo, or the Chinese state airline, Air China."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list"]," has banned Air Koryo from operating commercial air services to the UK, with the exception of 2 Tupolev Tu204 aircraft. The Department for Transport maintains the list, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents on Air Koryo flights reported in July 2016 and May 2017 highlight concerns about Air Koryo’s safety record and maintenance standards."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flooding is common in the rainy season from July to August. This can disrupt travel, especially to rural areas. Check that routes are passable before setting out on long journeys."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for North Korea","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/119/north-korea#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in North Korea","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/119/north-korea"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of North Korea. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Japanese encephalitis occurs, especially during the summer."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cholera also occurs and all water is a potential health risk. You should drink and use only boiled or bottled water and avoid ice in drinks. Tuberculosis is also common."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Basic medication including antibiotics is sometimes unavailable in North Korea."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries. Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in North Korea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Health facilities in North Korea are poor. Standards of clinical hygiene in hospitals are low. Anaesthetics are sometimes unavailable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Evacuation is likely to be necessary for serious illness or injury. Avoid surgery if at all possible. Facilities for dental treatment are also poor."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["help and services in North Korea","https://www.gov.uk/world/north-korea"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/north-korea/british-embassy-pyongyang"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/north-korea/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":15692,"change":"New information about dual nationals returning to the UK (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"07296213ee6d00d2eae29dd3eb815a8c2fa55f84f9ebea56a7ee07970adc0904","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/peru","bytes":116495,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Peru travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-07T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-06T16:13:51+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Within 20km south of the Peru-Colombia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km south of the Putumayo River and the border between Peru and Colombia (Loreto region) except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Amazon River"]},{"k":"li","s":["the area of the triple border with Brazil and Colombia from and including the towns of Caballococha in Peru up to the actual triple border at Santa Rosa de Yavari town"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Valley of the Apurímac, Ene, and Mantaro Rivers (VRAEM)"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Valley of the Apurímac, Ene, and Mantaro Rivers, also known as the VRAEM region."]},{"k":"p","s":["We advise against all but essential travel to these two areas for safety and security reasons."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pop Leo XIV visit to Peru"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pope Leo XIV will visit Peru from 11-16 November. During the visit, please expect increased security measures, road closures, traffic disruption, and large public gatherings. Cusco Airport will be closed on 15 November from 7am to 3pm local time. Please check with your airline before travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. If you have onward travel plans within the region, check travel advice for all destinations you plan to travel through. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Peru’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Peru set and enforce entry rules. If you are not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Peruvian Consulate General in the UK (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Peru, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel to Peru without a visa for tourism or short visits. If you are travelling for any other reason, check requirements with the Peruvian Consulate General in the UK (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"p","s":["When you arrive in Peru, you will normally get permission to stay for up to 90 days in a 180 day period. The 180 day period is calculated from the date of your first entry into Peru. Immigration officials can grant you a maximum of 183 days in a 365 day period as a visitor or tourist."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay, you will get a fine and you could be detained."]},{"k":"h","s":["Arriving at an international airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you arrive in Peru at an international airport, authorities will register your entry digitally through a Tarjeta Andina de Migración (TAM) - a virtual immigration control document."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can check how long you are allowed to stay in Peru on the ",["Superintendencia Nacional de Migraciones","https://cel.migraciones.gob.pe/ConsultaTAMVirtual/VerificarTAM"]," website (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Airport fee"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 7 December, passengers transiting or connecting through Lima (Jorge Chávez International) Airport will be required to pay a fee, known as a TUUA (Tarifa Unica por Uso de Aeropuerto, or Airport Use Fee)."]},{"k":"p","s":["This fee is not currently included in airline tickets."]},{"k":"p","s":["To avoid delays, travellers are encouraged to pay in advance via the ",["Lima Airport online platform","https://pagotuua.lima-airport.com/"]," or use available on-site payment options, including mobile POS (Point of Sale) agents, dedicated payment modules, and QR codes."]},{"k":"h","s":["Arriving by land"]},{"k":"p","s":["Land entry: make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter Peru by land from a neighbouring country, get a passport entry stamp at the immigration checkpoint. You cannot leave Peru without one. If you did not get a stamp, ",["apply to get a passport entry stamp online","https://agenciavirtual.migraciones.gob.pe/agencia-virtual/identidad"]," (form in Spanish) and:"]},{"k":"li","s":["give your passport details"]},{"k":"li","s":["give evidence of your entry to Peru, such as a bus ticket in your name"]},{"k":"li","s":["show an exit stamp from the last country you visited"]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy can help you to apply for an entry stamp. You should start this process as soon as possible."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you cannot give the information needed, you must apply for an exit order or expulsion order to leave Peru in person at the ",["Immigration Office in Lima","https://www.gob.pe/migraciones"],". These orders may stop you from re-entering Peru for a number of years. The British Embassy cannot intervene in these decisions but can help you with the exit procedure."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling inside Peru without a passport"]},{"k":"p","s":["If your passport is lost or stolen and you plan to travel inside Peru, contact your travel agency, airline or bus company to check their requirements. Some companies will not allow you to travel carrying a police report only. You may need a new passport or an ",["emergency travel document","https://www.gov.uk/travel-urgently-from-abroad-without-uk-passport"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Peru guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/177/peru#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children aged 17 and under who are travelling on a British passport and have Peruvian resident status need written permission (‘Autorización de Viaje Notarial’) from the non-accompanying parent or parents to leave Peru."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get permission in a letter signed by a public notary in Peru. The letter must include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["proposed destination"]},{"k":"li","s":["purpose of the trip"]},{"k":"li","s":["departure date"]},{"k":"li","s":["return date"]},{"k":"p","s":["These requirements do not normally apply to children with tourist status, but immigration officers may ask for them in circumstances considered suspicious, or if the child has overstayed in Peru and the stay lasts more than 183 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information, contact the Peruvian Consulate General in the UK (in Spanish) or the ",["Peruvian Immigration Department","https://www.gob.pe/migraciones"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Peru","https://www.gob.pe/6997-mercancias-restringidas-y-prohibidas#main"]," (in Spanish). You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can bring one laptop and 2 mobile phones into Peru without paying tax."]},{"k":"p","s":["When you leave Peru, you may be stopped and prosecuted if you are carrying:"]},{"k":"li","s":["products made from wild animal skins"]},{"k":"li","s":["crafts made with preserved butterflies, spiders, starfish, sea horses or other fish or insects"]},{"k":"li","s":["crafts and jewellery made with condor or other wild bird feathers, turtle shells, teeth, bones and other animal parts"]},{"k":"p","s":["The sale of souvenirs made with wild animal parts, including condor feathers, is illegal in Peru. These products are often sold in tourist markets in Cusco and Iquitos."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to remove any archaeological artefacts from Peru without authorisation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Peru","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Peru"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Peru cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Political protests in Peru are unpredictable and can escalate quickly. Demonstrations can become violent and lead to roadblocks, travel disruption, including trains, and suspension of immigration services at land borders. This is often without notice or notification of estimated re-opening timelines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Local groups can announce strike action, with little or no notice, particularly in areas connected to mining. These may quickly spill over from one region to another."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal for foreigners in Peru to participate in political activities, including demonstrations against the government. You may face detention or deportation if you take part in a demonstration. To reduce any risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid large gatherings and protests"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay in a safe place"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the instructions of army or police officers"]},{"k":"li","s":["take the advice of local authorities or tour operators"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media, including social media channels"]},{"k":"li","s":["be wary of unverified, unofficial information"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you travel with enough food, water, local currency and personal medication"]},{"k":"li","s":["allow extra time to reach your destination"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests in Lima often happen in the historic centre, where access can be restricted, but they can also spread to other areas. Other regions that have seen recent protests include Arequipa, Ayacucho, Cusco, La Libertad, Madre de Dios and Puno."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some train services in the south, including those to and from Machu Picchu, are occasionally suspended or disrupted because of protests. Contact your travel provider for further advice on disruptions, and check if changes need to be made to your journey."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact the ",["iPeru information service","https://www.peru.travel/en/useful-data/iperu"]," for help with issues travelling to different regions of Peru."]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy’s ability to provide help will be very limited where protests or criminal activity disrupt travel or damage infrastructure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Help from local authorities, including police and emergency services, will also be very limited, especially if airports, roads and railroads are affected."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Organised crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a higher risk to your safety in areas where there is serious organised crime linked to drug production. This includes the border areas with Ecuador, Colombia and Brazil and the Valley of Apurímac, Ene and Mantaro rivers (VRAEM). Remnants of the Shining Path guerrilla group are still active in some of the main coca growing areas in central Peru (Alto Huallaga, Aguaytia and VRAEM river basins)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Street crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Street crime, including muggings and thefts, is a significant problem in Lima, Cusco, Arequipa and other major cities. Be alert in public places and when withdrawing cash from ATMs."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is safer to use ATMs inside banks, supermarkets or large commercial buildings during business hours. Do not walk on your own in quiet areas or at night."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been a number of robberies at gunpoint of British tourists and residents. Attacks can take place in tourist areas of Lima such as Miraflores and Barranco. To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid wearing or displaying expensive items"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid using your phone at the roadside, as motorbike riders may snatch it"]},{"k":"li","s":["report crimes to local police as soon as possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask lodge or hotel staff for help if an incident happens on site"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals target cars stopped at traffic lights. Keep your doors locked and windows shut while driving."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Petty crime, such as pickpocketing and bag-snatching, is common, so:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your belongings secure"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not leave bags unattended"]},{"k":"li","s":["on bus journeys, keep your passport with you"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Fake taxi drivers"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of robbery by criminals posing as taxi drivers, especially at Jorge Chavez International Airport and bus terminals. Fake taxi drivers and thieves pretending to be tour operators sometimes approach arriving passengers. To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["use licensed telephone or app-based taxi services"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not hail taxis on the street"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask your hotel to book taxis for you"]},{"k":"li","s":["use one of the ",["official taxi companies at the airport","https://www.lima-airport.com/en/cms/pasajeros/transport/taxis"],", located at desks directly outside the baggage hall"]},{"k":"li","s":["use one of the taxis registered at bus terminals"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Kidnappings and hold-ups"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists, especially those travelling alone, are at risk of ‘express kidnapping’. Victims are taken hostage and forced to withdraw money from ATMs for their release, usually at night. Incidents often involve armed criminals posing as taxi drivers, or taxi drivers working for organised gangs. Armed robbers sometimes hold up provincial and inter-city buses."]},{"k":"p","s":["If a kidnapping or hold-up happens to you:"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not attempt to resist attackers"]},{"k":"li","s":["agree to any demands for cash or goods"]},{"k":"li","s":["report the incident to the police as soon as possible"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals can also fake kidnappings by contacting the numbers from a stolen mobile phone and claiming to have kidnapped the owner. They then demand a ransom. Report it to the police if you suspect this has taken place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Personal attacks, including sexual assaults, are infrequent but do happen, mostly in the Cusco and Arequipa areas. Unscrupulous tour agents have targeted young females, travelling alone in the Cusco area. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["buy your own drinks and always keep sight of them"]},{"k":"li","s":["try to get help from people you know"]},{"k":"li","s":["report incidents to the police as soon as possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["advice for women travelling and living abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"p","s":["For information on reputable tourist services around Peru, contact the ",["iPeru information service","https://www.peru.travel/en/useful-data/iperu"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been deaths and cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in Peru."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Counterfeit US and Peruvian banknotes are in circulation. There have been reports of street money changers in Cusco tourist areas fraudulently using Peruvian intis (former currency now out of circulation)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry ID with you. The Peruvian police may ask to see ID; if you do not have it with you, you may be required to go to the nearest police station."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drug use and drug trafficking in Peru carry lengthy jail sentences. Prison conditions in Peru are extremely poor and the British Embassy cannot intervene in police or judicial matters, or secure more favourable conditions."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["pack your luggage yourself and always keep it with you"]},{"k":"li","s":["not carry anything through customs for anyone"]},{"k":"li","s":["not take coca leaves or coca tea out of the country – it is illegal to import these items into the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drug couriers have targeted British nationals with email scams. These criminals will try to get you to travel to Peru to pick up items containing drugs. You’ll face detention for drug trafficking if convicted."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Military photography"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take photographs of anything of a military nature, it is illegal and you could face a prison sentence of two to five years."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Peru, but social attitudes are generally conservative. Crimes against the LGBT+ community are not included in hate crime legislation and same-sex partnerships are not formally recognised."]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex couples showing affection in public may receive unwanted and negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your insurance covers you for all planned activities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Unregulated tour services"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure that agencies providing adventure activities like zipline, canopy tours, bungee jumping, paragliding, kayaking, rock climbing, sand buggies and surfing have a licence. You should also check their health and safety precautions. For updated information on tour and sport services, contact the ",["iPeru information service","https://www.peru.travel/en/useful-data/iperu"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["Peru’s highest peaks are in the Cordillera Blanca Mountains. Several hikers have died and others had to be rescued after serious accidents. Much of the region is inaccessible by helicopter so rescues are usually carried out on foot. Contact the ",["iPeru information service","https://www.peru.travel/en/useful-data/iperu"]," in Huaraz – phone: 0051 (43) 428 812 – before you set off."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sand buggies"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been deaths and accidents involving recreational sand buggies, particularly in the sand dunes around Ica and Lake Huacachina. These buggies are unregulated, and the drivers and agencies take no responsibility for the welfare of passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Surfing"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are unauthorised surfboard rentals at the beaches of Miraflores. There may not be lifeguards on beaches."]},{"k":"hs","s":["River rafting and Amazon riverboat cruises"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information or to check the credentials of rafting and cruise operators, contact iPeru information service."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information about the risks of travelling in the Amazon region, see ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Spiritual cleansing"]},{"k":"p","s":["Shamans and other people offer ‘spiritual cleansing’ (Ayahuasca or San Pedro) to tourists in the Amazon area, northern Peru and Cusco. This often involves drinking a brew containing dimethyltryptamine (DMT), a hallucinogenic drug that is a Class A substance in the UK. This brew is not regulated and its effect on existing medical conditions is not well understood. People have become seriously ill and, in some cases, died after taking part. Spiritual cleansing retreats are usually far from populated areas, making it difficult to get medical attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have also been reports of sexual assault during these ceremonies. For guidance to support you if you have been sexually assaulted or raped in Peru ",["see Getting help","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru/getting-help"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Peru, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Peru for up to 6 months if your immigration stay permit is valid. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport or valid ID (‘carne de extranjería’ if you are a resident) when driving."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care if you are driving close to places where protests are taking place. Do not attempt to pass blockades."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards in Peru are poor. Drivers often ignore stop signs and traffic lights, and fatal crashes are frequent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drivers do not always show concern for pedestrians. You should be extra cautious when walking alongside traffic."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bus crashes are common, especially at night. Only use reputable transport companies, and where possible, avoid overnight travel, especially in mountainous and remote regions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["El Niño 2026-2027"]},{"k":"p","s":["Through late 2026 to April 2027, the El Niño weather event is expected to generate heavy rainfall, possible flooding, landslides, and mudslides, especially in, but not restricted to, the northern and central coast. These could cause travel disruption, such as road closures, and affect access to essential services."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should monitor local news and weather reports and the latest information about ",["road alerts","https://alertasviales.sutran.gob.pe/"]," (Spanish only)."]},{"k":"p","s":["For official updates on El Niño, please visit the Peruvian government website: ",["ENFEN","https://enfen.imarpe.gob.pe/"]," (Spanish only), and check Real-time road updates (Spanish only)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rainy season"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season in Peru runs from November to May. There is heavy rain and snow in northern Peru, the Andes, including Cusco, and other parts of the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season can disrupt:"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel services"]},{"k":"li","s":["road travel between provinces"]},{"k":"li","s":["flights"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourist sites"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rockslides, mudslides and snow can disrupt walking routes, road and rail travel in mountain and jungle areas:"]},{"k":"li","s":["across the Cusco Region"]},{"k":"li","s":["routes to Machu Picchu, including the alternative Santa Maria-Santa Teresa-hydroelectric plant route, and the Salkantay route"]},{"k":"li","s":["the route to Manu, in Cusco and Madre de Dios"]},{"k":"li","s":["across northern regions"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest conditions with your tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel with enough food, water, cash in local currency, medication and warm clothes"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media for updates on travel information before starting your journey"]},{"k":"li","s":["contact the iPeru information service before you set off"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Peru is in an active earthquake zone and there are frequent tremors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow advice given by the local authorities. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to visit areas of known volcanic activity, listen to all warnings and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Peru’s most active volcano, Ubinas, has been emitting gas and ash recently, leading to some local villages being evacuated, affecting 30,000 people."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after a volcanic eruption","https://www.ready.gov/volcanoes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tsunamis and high tides"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although tsunamis are rare in Peru, higher tides often happen either after an earthquake or for other reasons throughout the year. See the Peruvian Directorate of Hydrography and Navigation (in Spanish) for information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Peru. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Peru-Colombia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km south of the Putumayo River and the border between Peru and Colombia (Loreto region) except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Amazon River"]},{"k":"li","s":["the area of the triple border with Brazil and Colombia from and including the towns of Caballococha in Peru up to the actual triple border at Santa Rosa de Yavari town"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is due to a high level of violence from organised criminal gangs who produce and traffic illegal drugs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Putumayo River"]},{"k":"p","s":["The advice against all but essential travel applies to the Peruvian side of the Putumayo riverbank, though not on the river itself. If you are planning to leave a boat on the Colombian side of the river, check ",["Colombia travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/colombia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Putumayo River forms most of Peru’s border with Colombia. The area is known for intensive cocaine and marijuana production. Drug trafficking and other violent organised crime takes place on and around the river."]},{"k":"h","s":["Valley of the Apurímac, Ene and Mantaro rivers (VRAEM)"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Valley of the Apurímac, Ene and Mantaro Rivers, also known as the VRAEM region."]},{"k":"p","s":["Remnants of the Shining Path guerrilla group occasionally attack the police, military forces and local authorities in this area. They do not usually target tourists. However, you could be a victim of violence due to mistaken identity or by getting caught up in a security incident involving others."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is little assistance available in this area from the Peruvian authorities, and any British Embassy assistance is severely limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["Note that some parts of the Apurimac River in the Departments of Cusco and Arequipa are not within the VRAEM."]},{"k":"h","s":["Amazon River"]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed criminals operate along the Amazon River and have targeted solo travellers and foreign nationals. These include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["thieves, known locally as ‘river pirates’"]},{"k":"li","s":["organised criminal gangs, who transport and smuggle illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel with a reputable commercial or travel company if you are visiting the Amazon River. Stay on your boat where it passes through areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is little assistance available in this area from the Peruvian authorities, and any British Embassy assistance is severely limited."]},{"k":"h","s":["States of emergency"]},{"k":"p","s":["States of emergency have been declared in some parts of Peru. You can read a list of the areas with a state of emergency in ",["El Peruano","https://diariooficial.elperuano.pe/Normas"]," official newspaper (in Spanish). For more information on your destination, contact the ",["iPeru information service","https://www.peru.travel/en/useful-data/iperu"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In these areas you may notice an increased security presence. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["comply with the instructions of local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid crowds"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor the situation closely"]},{"k":"h","s":["Peru-Ecuador border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Peruvian government has taken preventive measures in northern Peru in response to the security situation in Ecuador. You may notice an increased security presence."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to northern Peru or plan to cross land border checkpoints, ensure you follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you wish to enter Ecuador by crossing a land border from Peru, you must show the Ecuadorean authorities certain documents. See ",["Ecuador travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only cross the Peru-Ecuador land border at official checkpoints. Other parts of the border may still have unexploded landmines. Some tourists have been robbed by fake taxi drivers. Be extremely vigilant in these areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is little assistance available in this area from the Peruvian authorities, and any British Embassy assistance is severely limited."]},{"k":"h","s":["Inca trail"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only basic medical services are available at Machu Picchu. Several climbers have died or suffered serious injuries after falling while climbing Huayna Picchu, a peak near Machu Picchu."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["always register when entering national parks"]},{"k":"li","s":["be particularly careful in steep and slippery areas, or those that are unfenced or unmarked"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ‘Inca Jungle Trail’ can be difficult for vehicles due to poor road conditions. There have been fatal road accidents."]},{"k":"h","s":["Lake Titicaca"]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed robbers have attacked travellers walking on their own. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["always take care"]},{"k":"li","s":["contact the local tourist information centre for advice about known safe zones"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel with a group at the southern end of Lake Titicaca if walking at night"]},{"k":"h","s":["Nazca Lines"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to fly over the Nazca Lines, check the airline company is licensed and has a good safety record before you book. There have been several fatal accidents in recent years."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ask the ",["iPeru information service","https://www.peru.travel/en/useful-data/iperu"]," for advice about booking flights."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 106 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you are referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Peru","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/177/peru#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Peru","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/177/peru"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Oropouche virus disease"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a serious risk in parts of Peru, including Cusco, Puno, the Colca Canyon and Kuelap. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Diarrhoea caused by contaminated food or water is common and is potentially serious. See more about food and water hygiene."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dengue outbreak"]},{"k":"p","s":["Peru is experiencing a major dengue outbreak following floods. See the ‘Outbreaks’ page of the ",["TravelHealthPro Peru guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/177/peru#Outbreaks"]," for more information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries. Many medications are available over the counter in Peru, but local prescriptions will be required for some."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Peru"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical treatment is not easily available and can be more difficult to access outside of Lima. Make sure you have appropriate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need emergency medical assistance during your trip in Lima, dial one of the following numbers: +51 1 416 6767 (Lima - Alerta Med), or +51 1 467 4861 (Lima - Clave Medica) and ask for an ambulance. These services are private, so you will need to pay for them."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Peru","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/peru-list-of-lawyers/list-of-medical-facilities-in-peru"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Peru"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 106"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 116"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 105"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Peru"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Peru"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Peru]"]," in Peru"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Peru","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/peru-bereavement-packinformation/peru-beravement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Peru","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/peru-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you are a ",["victim of rape or sexual assault","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/sexual-assault-in-peru"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you are a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you are ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/peru/british-embassy-lima"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Peru","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-peru"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":30282,"change":"New information about Pope Leo XIV’s visit to Peru from 11-16 November, including increased security measures and travel disruption (’Warnings and insurance’ page)."}};
